  "response_text": "If __set_PSP(stackptr) is not included in the code, the SVC still tries to pop the stack frame but it does so from MSP which is the wrong stack to be popped. Garbage values are loaded into the registers such as PC, LR and xPSR. The value in PC is garbage hence the CPU raises a hard fault.\\nIf we did not set PSP then the wrong registers would be read while the program runs causing an invalid address or alignment error and resulting in a hard fault. This is because the PC\u2019s contents would be different and thus the print continuously function would not run. Additionally, the other registers will be overwritten which will result in a hard fault. If we did not set PSP, the CPU would still be using the MSP.\\n",
